# UNRAID: preserve upstream line endings exactly as committed.
#
# A few upstream files (e.g. src/driveformatthread.h) are committed with CRLF.
# If a tool silently normalises them to LF, every line shows as changed and the
# file conflicts wholesale on the next upstream rebase — the exact churn
# PORTING.md exists to prevent. Treating sources as binary-ish for EOL purposes
# means git never rewrites endings on checkout or commit.
* -text
